meta {
  name: 1 Book appointment
  type: http
  seq: 1
}
post {
  url: {{bookingUrl}}/api/v1/booking/appointments
  body: json
}
body:json {
  {
    "emailProvider": "{{providerEmail}}",
    "emailCustomer": "{{customerEmail}}",
    "start": "2026-09-01T10:00:00Z",
    "end": "2026-09-01T11:00:00Z",
    "appointmentDescription": "Local test appointment"
  }
}
docs {
  Guarded with `AssertOwnerAny(emailProvider, emailCustomer)` — **either** party may act on the
  appointment, so you can run this logged in as the provider or the customer. A third party gets `403`.

  ⚠️ Validation runs before the guard, so an invalid body returns `400` and never reaches it.
}
